course: dictionary
lesson: 2652
title: Detour: the longer way round
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A detour is a longer or different way you take to avoid something, such as a closed road or a traffic jam. Context helps you find this meaning: «The road was closed, so we had to take a detour through the hills.» The closed road tells you the detour is a way round the problem.
explain: A detour can also be a trip off your main route to visit somewhere. «Make a detour to see the waterfall» means you leave your main route for a sight. Here the clue is «to see the waterfall»: nothing is blocking the way, you just choose to go there.
explain: Detour can be a verb too. To detour means to go a different way, or to send traffic a different way. Road signs say «Detour» in the US and «Diversion» in the UK, and both mean the same thing.
fact: A detour is a longer or different way round something.
fact: «Take a detour» and «make a detour» are common phrases.
fact: In a maths problem, a detour adds extra distance: if the normal route is 10 km and the detour adds 3 km, the trip is 13 km.
fact: In stories, a detour often leads to an adventure.
fact: «Detour» (US road sign) and «diversion» (UK road sign) mean the same thing.
exercise: «The road was closed, so we had to take a detour through the hills.» What is a detour here? | *A longer, different way round the closed road | A type of hill | A short cut straight through the road | A sign that says stop
exercise: A trip is 10 km, and a detour adds 3 km. How long is the trip now? | 3 km | 30 km | *13 km | 7 km
exercise: On a UK road, which word is on the sign for a detour? | *Diversion | Closed | Detour | Shortcut
test: In «make a detour to see the waterfall», what is the detour for? | *A trip off the main route to visit somewhere | To go faster | To avoid a closed road | To lose sight of something
test: Yesterday the bus ___ through the village because of roadworks. Which form of detour fits? | *Detoured | Detouring | Detour | Detours
exam: Ella says a detour is always a short cut. What is the right meaning? | It is a sign that says stop | *It is a longer or different way round something | It is a type of road | Yes, it is always shorter
